Article 2 (Fact-Finding Surveys on Households Supporting Parents, etc.)
(1) The fact-finding survey of households supporting parents, etc. under Article 6 (3) of the Act on Encouragement and Support for Filial Piety (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall include the following matters:
1. The composition and family relationships of households supporting parents, etc.;
2. The economic conditions, including income and assets, and housing of households supporting parents, etc.;
3. Patterns of support provided to parents, etc.;
4. Awareness of and attitudes toward supporting parents, etc.;
5. Demand for support for parents, etc.;
6. Other matters that need to be investigated concerning households supporting parents, etc.
(2) The State and local governments may commission a specialized research institution, organization, or relevant expert to conduct a fact-finding survey under paragraph (1).
